---
/**
 * /redazione: the kit a volunteer hands to an AI before writing.
 *
 * One prompt, one button. There used to be three, one per content type, and
 * making a volunteer classify their own task before they had written anything
 * was a decision they should never have been asked to make: the instructions
 * tell the model how to tell a new post from an edit, which is its job.
 *
 * ## The shape of the flow
 *
 * The prompt names `/redazione/istruzioni.txt`, which `robots.txt` allows even
 * on a preview host, so an assistant reads the rules itself rather than being
 * fed fifteen kilobytes. The answer comes back as a whole `.mdx` file, and
 * Keystatic's "Paste entry" fills every field from it: verified on production,
 * including the category, the event checkbox and its dates.
 *
 * The full instructions are still on the page, behind the disclosure, because a
 * free tier usually cannot open a link at all and the short prompt tells the
 * model to say so rather than guess.
 *
 * ## Why a textarea and not a code block
 *
 * It is the no-JavaScript path: without the script a volunteer can still tap
 * into the box and copy by hand, which a `<pre>` on a phone makes miserable.
 * What is in it is exactly what the model receives.
 *
 * ## Why it is noindex and out of the sitemap
 *
 * Same reason as /styleguide: a tool for the people who run the site, not a
 * page of it.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import H2 from '../../components/H2.astro';
import { linkPrompt, prompt } from '../../lib/authoring';
import pasteButton from '../../assets/redazione/paste-entry.png';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://www.ventorelativo.it');

const short = linkPrompt(site);
const full = prompt(site);
const keystatic = new URL('/keystatic', site).href;
/* Straight to the empty form, which saves a volunteer two steps. The branch
   segment is not optional: in GitHub mode `/keystatic/collection/news/create`
   answers "Not found", checked on the deployed admin. */
const newsForm = new URL('/keystatic/branch/main/collection/news/create', site).href;
const plainText = new URL('/redazione/istruzioni.txt', site).href;
const asJson = new URL('/redazione/contenuti.json', site).href;

/**
 * Where the prompt can be sent, chosen once and remembered.
 *
 * The `?q=` carries the short prompt: the full instructions are 26,736
 * characters encoded and Google answers 400 to a Gemini URL somewhere between
 * 8k and 20k. The same click copies it, so when the parameter is ignored, and
 * it is undocumented on all three, the result is an empty chat and a full
 * clipboard rather than a dead end.
 */
const CHATS = [
  { id: 'chatgpt', name: 'ChatGPT', href: 'https://chatgpt.com/?q=' },
  { id: 'claude', name: 'Claude', href: 'https://claude.ai/new?q=' },
  { id: 'gemini', name: 'Gemini', href: 'https://gemini.google.com/app?q=' },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Redazione"
  description="Come scrivere una news o correggere una pagina del sito con l'aiuto di un'intelligenza artificiale."
  intro="Scrivi una news, annuncia un evento o correggi una scheda, facendoti aiutare da ChatGPT, Gemini o Claude. Funziona anche con gli account gratuiti."
  noindex
>
  <div class="prose">
    <H2>Come funziona</H2>

    <ol>
      <li>Dici qui sotto quale intelligenza artificiale usi. Il sito se lo ricorda.</li>
      <li>Premi il pulsante: copia il prompt e apre la chat.</li>
      <li>
        Incolli il prompt e sotto scrivi quello che sai: appunti, il messaggio che ti è
        arrivato, quello che c'è sulla locandina. Anche in disordine.
      </li>
      <li>Ti risponde con il testo pronto. Lo copi e lo porti nel sito.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="picker field">
    <label for="ai">Quale intelligenza artificiale usi?</label>
    <select id="ai">
      <option value="copia">Nessuna, copio soltanto</option>
      {
        CHATS.map((chat) => (
          <option value={chat.id} data-url={chat.href}>
            {chat.name}
          </option>
        ))
      }
    </select>
    <noscript>
      Senza JavaScript il pulsante non funziona: seleziona il testo nella casella e
      copialo a mano.
    </noscript>
  </div>

  <section class="kit">
    <div class="field">
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="prompt">Il prompt da copiare</label>
      {
        /* `set:text` rather than a child: an expression inside the tag would put
          the JSX indentation into the value the volunteer copies. */
      }
      <textarea class="kit__text" readonly rows="5" id="prompt" set:text={short} />
    </div>

    <p class="kit__actions">
      <button class="button" type="button" data-copy="prompt" data-open>
        Copia il prompt
      </button>
    </p>

    <details class="kit__full">
      <summary>L'intelligenza artificiale non riesce ad aprire il link?</summary>
      <p>
        Capita con gli account gratuiti, che spesso non leggono le pagine web. Copia
        questo e incollalo nella stessa conversazione: sono le stesse istruzioni, per
        intero.
      </p>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="pieno">Le istruzioni complete</label>
        <textarea class="kit__text" readonly rows="8" id="pieno" set:text={full} />
      </div>
      <p class="kit__actions">
        <button class="button button--outline" type="button" data-copy="pieno">
          Copia le istruzioni complete
        </button>
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <H2>Portare il testo nel sito</H2>

    <p>
      Per una <strong>news nuova</strong> l'intelligenza artificiale ti dà un blocco di testo
      che comincia con tre trattini. Copialo tutto, apri <a href={newsForm}
        >il modulo di una news nuova</a
      > e in alto a destra premi <strong>Paste entry</strong>: tutti i campi si
      riempiono da soli.
    </p>

    <figure class="shot">
      <Image
        src={pasteButton}
        alt="I pulsanti in alto a destra nel gestore dei contenuti: un orologio, due icone a forma di appunti e il pulsante blu Create"
        widths={[310, 620]}
        sizes="310px"
        quality={90}
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Paste entry</strong> è la seconda icona a forma di appunti, subito prima del
        pulsante blu <strong>Create</strong>. La prima volta il browser chiede il
        permesso di leggere gli appunti: rispondi <strong>Allow</strong>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>Restano due cose da fare a mano:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        premere il pulsante con le frecce circolari accanto a <strong
          >Indirizzo (URL)</strong
        >, che si scrive da solo a partire dal titolo;
      </li>
      <li>caricare la foto e incollare il testo alternativo.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Per una <strong>correzione</strong> a una pagina o a una scheda che esiste già non c'è
      un blocco da incollare: ricevi l'elenco dei campi da cambiare, apri <a
        href={keystatic}>il gestore dei contenuti</a
      > e cambi solo quelli. Se l'intelligenza artificiale ti chiede com'è il testo adesso
      è normale, non può vederlo: selezionalo nel riquadro grande, copialo e incollaglielo.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Rileggi prima di salvare.</strong> Un'intelligenza artificiale sbaglia le date
      con la faccia di chi le sa: controlla date e luoghi contro i tuoi appunti. Quello che
      salvi va online in un paio di minuti.
    </p>

    <H2>Le istruzioni da sole</H2>
    <p>
      Le regole che l'intelligenza artificiale legge, se ti servono in chiaro: <a
        href={plainText}>istruzioni.txt</a
      >. Le stesse in forma di dati, per chi collega il sito a un programma: <a
        href={asJson}>contenuti.json</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  /*
    One remembered choice, one button.

    The date is prepended here rather than baked into the page because the page
    is built once and read for months: a model told the wrong date will happily
    decide next Saturday's event already happened. `Intl` gives the Italian
    spelling for free.

    No import, so Astro keeps this inline: on a page nobody but an editor opens
    it would still be an extra request. See AGENTS.md, known traps.
  */
  const KEY = 'redazione-ai';

  const today = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('it-IT', { dateStyle: 'full' }).format(
    new Date(),
  );

  const select = document.getElementById('ai') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const buttons = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]')];
  /* Only the primary button opens a chat and takes the chosen service's name;
     the one behind the disclosure keeps its own label. */
  const opens = (button: HTMLButtonElement) => button.hasAttribute('data-open');

  const chosen = () => select.options[select.selectedIndex];

  /* Both directions wrapped: a browser set to block site data throws on read
     as well as on write, and losing a preference must not break the button. */
  const remember = (value: string) => {
    try {
      localStorage.setItem(KEY, value);
    } catch {
      /* Private mode, or site data blocked. The choice lasts this visit. */
    }
  };

  const label = () => {
    const chat = chosen();
    const text =
      chat.value === 'copia' ? 'Copia il prompt' : `Copia e apri ${chat.text}`;
    for (const button of buttons) if (opens(button)) button.textContent = text;
  };

  try {
    const saved = localStorage.getItem(KEY);
    if (saved && [...select.options].some((option) => option.value === saved)) {
      select.value = saved;
    }
  } catch {
    /* Nothing saved, or nothing readable. The default option stands. */
  }

  label();

  select.addEventListener('change', () => {
    remember(select.value);
    label();
  });

  /*
    Copy, without ever throwing.

    `navigator.clipboard` does not exist on an insecure origin, and `npm run
    dev` advertises `http://192.168.x.x:4321` beside localhost. Opened at that
    address, the first line of this handler threw, so nothing was copied *and*
    no tab opened: the broken half took the working half with it.

    `execCommand` is deprecated and is the only thing that copies there. It
    works on the selection and the box does not hold the date line, so the
    value is swapped for one synchronous call and put back before anything can
    paint.
  */
  const copy = (box: HTMLTextAreaElement, text: string) => {
    try {
      if (navigator.clipboard?.writeText) return navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);

      const original = box.value;
      box.value = text;
      box.select();
      /* Cast because the deprecation is the point: `astro check` flags the
         real signature, and there is no replacement that copies on an
         insecure origin. */
      const legacy = document as unknown as { execCommand(command: string): boolean };
      const ok = legacy.execCommand('copy');
      box.value = original;
      return ok ? Promise.resolve() : Promise.reject(new Error('copy refused'));
    } catch (error) {
      return Promise.reject(error);
    }
  };

  for (const button of buttons) {
    const own = button.textContent;
    const restore = () => {
      if (opens(button)) label();
      else button.textContent = own;
    };

    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const box = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy!) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
      const chat = chosen();

      /*
        Order matters. The copy starts first, inside the gesture and while the
        document still has focus; `window.open` follows in the same turn, so
        the popup blocker sees a real click. Awaiting the copy before opening
        would lose the gesture and the tab with it.
      */
      const text = `Oggi è ${today}.\n\n${box.value}`;
      const copied = copy(box, text);

      if (opens(button) && chat.value !== 'copia') {
        window.open(chat.dataset.url + encodeURIComponent(text), '_blank', 'noopener');
      }

      copied
        .then(() => {
          button.textContent = 'Copiato';
          setTimeout(restore, 2000);
        })
        .catch(() => {
          /* Refused, usually because the new tab took the focus. Leave the
             text selected so one keystroke still gets it. */
          box.focus();
          box.select();
          button.textContent = 'Premi Ctrl+C';
        });
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .picker {
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block: var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
  }

  .picker select {
    /* `.field` styles inputs and textareas; a select is not one of them, and
       adding it there would reach into the CMS's own controls. */
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font: inherit;
  }

  .picker select:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus);
    outline-offset: 1px;
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .picker noscript {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .kit {
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .kit__text {
    /* Monospace so a stray character is visible, and small: this is a block to
       be copied, not to be read closely. */
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
    /* Grows to its content, so the short prompt is readable whole instead of
       cut mid-sentence, and the full instructions stop at the cap and scroll.
       `rows` is the fallback where this is not supported yet. */
    field-sizing: content;
    max-height: 40vh;
    resize: vertical;
    /* Wrap rather than scroll sideways: a soft wrap does not alter `value`,
       so what is copied is still the text as written. */
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }

  .kit__actions {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .kit__full {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .kit__full summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .kit__full summary:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .kit__full > p {
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .shot {
    margin-block: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* The screenshot is of a dark admin: a border keeps it from bleeding into a
     light page, and the radius matches the toolbar it was cut from. */
  .shot :global(img) {
    width: 310px;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .shot figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
